Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_root_the_table_accepts_never_overflows_returning_a_grandchild`.

The defect: a root whose page range runs past the top of the page numbers is accepted. Every end
the table computes below it (a child's end, a bounds report, a spent figure) can then overflow.

Expected to fail: an overflow check inside a call on the root the harness builds at the top of the
page numbers, or the harness's own "a root that fits was refused" assertion is never reached.

